  "description": "Compound-shift NF decomposition for atoms A=2..6 at 50-dps mpmath precision (no floats in emitted values). Composes the closed-form atomic shift (shift(Z,N) = 18Z + 21N + 1, prop:per-nucleon-shift-additive-linearity, PR #539 / w3-w4) with the interface α(I) contributions per canonical pppnnn ordering. NF coefficients at q_0 are computed in mpmath (port of hecke_core.build_atom_nf with mp.mpf arithmetic). LP active-set discovery uses scipy linprog as a discrete oracle, but every numerical field (y_0, y_*, x_*, primal_obj, dual_obj, duality_gap) is recomputed in mpmath via a high-precision linear-system solve restricted to the active basis. Also verifies the α_EM⁻¹ = q · [9]_q · [10]_q chain at 50 dps.",
